IMPORT prelude

-- Arbitration Act 2001 (Singapore) -- when the Act applies (s 3), the writing requirement (s 4), staying court proceedings (s 6),
-- the default tribunal (ss 12, 13), challenging an arbitrator (ss 14, 15), the arbitrator's and institution's immunity (ss 20, 59),
-- jurisdiction pleas (s 21), reasons and costs (ss 38, 39), correction of awards (s 43), enforcement (s 46), and the two ways to
-- attack an award in court: setting aside (s 48) and appeal on a question of law (ss 49, 50).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AA2001.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 5 of 2025 (in force 9 March 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a party or its lawyer
-- meets: the gateway, the agreement, the stay, the default tribunal, challenges, immunities, the award, and the two court routes
-- against it, with their deadlines. Not encoded: interpleader (s 8), extension of time (ss 10, 36), limitation (s 11), the conduct of
-- proceedings (Part 7), interest (s 35), arbitrator fees and withholding the award (ss 40, 41), preliminary points of law (s 45),
-- intellectual property disputes (Part 9A), privacy of proceedings (ss 56, 57), mediation (ss 62, 63), and anything in the Rules of
-- Court.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Arbitration Act 2001 -- agreements, tribunals and awards`

§§ `3 and 46(3) -- when the Act applies, and enforcement`

-- s 3: "This Act applies to any arbitration where the place of arbitration is Singapore and where Part 2 of the International
-- Arbitration Act 1994 does not apply to that arbitration."
-- s 46(1): an award made pursuant to an arbitration agreement "may, with permission of the Court, be enforced in the same manner as a
-- judgment"; (3) "Despite section 3, subsection (1) applies to an award irrespective of whether the place of arbitration is Singapore
-- or elsewhere."
GIVEN `seated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to the arbitration` IF
    `seated in Singapore` AND (NOT `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act applies`)

GIVEN `made pursuant to an arbitration agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `seated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the award may be enforced with permission under section 46` IF
    `made pursuant to an arbitration agreement`

§§ `4 -- the arbitration agreement must be in writing`

-- s 4(3): "An arbitration agreement must be in writing." (4) it is in writing "if its content is recorded in any form, whether or not
-- the arbitration agreement or contract has been concluded orally, by conduct or by other means". (5) an electronic communication
-- suffices "if the information contained in the electronic communication is accessible so as to be useable for subsequent
-- reference". (6) an assertion of an agreement in a pleading that calls for a reply and "is not denied" -- "there is deemed to be an
-- effective arbitration agreement". (7), (8) a reference in a contract (or a bill of lading) to a document containing an arbitration
-- clause is an agreement in writing "if the reference is such as to make that clause part of the contract".
DECLARE `Agreement facts` HAS
    `content recorded in any form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is in writing` IF
        `the facts`'s `content recorded in any form`
    OR  `the facts`'s `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference`
    OR  `the facts`'s `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is an effective arbitration agreement` IF
        `the agreement is in writing` `the facts`
    OR  `the facts`'s `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied`

§§ `6 -- staying court proceedings`

-- s 6(1): a party may apply for a stay "at any time after filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest and before
-- delivering any pleading (other than a pleading asserting that the court does not have jurisdiction in the proceedings) or taking any
-- other step in the proceedings". (2) the court "may" stay if satisfied (a) "there is no sufficient reason why the matter should not be
-- referred" and (b) the applicant was and remains "ready and willing to do all things necessary to the proper conduct of the
-- arbitration". (4) where no party has taken a further step "for a period of not less than 2 years" after a stay, the court may on its
-- own motion discontinue the proceedings.
GIVEN `filed and served a notice of intention` IS A BOOLEAN, `delivered a pleading on the merits` IS A BOOLEAN, `took another step in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stay application is in time` IF
    `filed and served a notice of intention` AND (NOT `delivered a pleading on the merits`) AND (NOT `took another step in the proceedings`)

GIVEN `application in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `sufficient reason against arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN, `ready and willing throughout` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may stay the proceedings` IF
    `application in time` AND (NOT `sufficient reason against arbitration`) AND `ready and willing throughout`

GIVEN `months with no step since the stay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may discontinue the stayed proceedings` IF
    `months with no step since the stay` AT LEAST 24

§§ `12, 13 -- the default tribunal`

-- s 12: "(1) The parties are free to determine the number of arbitrators. (2) Failing such determination, there is to be a single
-- arbitrator."
-- s 13(4): with no agreed procedure and 3 arbitrators, "(a) if a party fails to appoint an arbitrator within 30 days of receipt of a
-- first request to do so from the other party" the appointment "is to be made, upon the request of a party, by the appointing
-- authority". (8) the appointing authority "is the president of the Court of Arbitration of the Singapore International Arbitration
-- Centre"; (9) the Chief Justice may appoint another person to exercise its powers [Act 5 of 2025].
GIVEN `the parties fixed a number` IS A BOOLEAN, `the number fixed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of arbitrators` MEANS
    IF `the parties fixed a number` THEN `the number fixed` ELSE 1

GIVEN `an agreed appointment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN, `the party has appointed` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the first request was received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointing authority may appoint the defaulting party's arbitrator` IF
    (NOT `an agreed appointment procedure`) AND (NOT `the party has appointed`) AND `days since the first request was received` GREATER THAN 30

§§ `14, 15 -- challenging an arbitrator`

-- s 14(3): an arbitrator may be challenged "only if" (a) circumstances give "rise to justifiable doubts as to his or her impartiality
-- or independence" or (b) "he or she does not possess the qualifications agreed to by the parties". (4) a party who appointed or
-- participated in appointing the arbitrator may challenge "only if the party becomes aware of any of the grounds ... after the
-- arbitrator has been appointed".
-- s 15(4): if the tribunal rejects the challenge the party "may, within 30 days after receiving notice of the decision rejecting the
-- challenge, apply to the Court"; (5) "No appeal shall lie" against the Court's decision.
GIVEN `justifiable doubts as to impartiality or independence` IS A BOOLEAN, `lacks the agreed qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN, `the challenger took part in the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN, `learned of the ground only after the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arbitrator may be challenged` IF
        (`justifiable doubts as to impartiality or independence` OR `lacks the agreed qualifications`)
    AND ((NOT `the challenger took part in the appointment`) OR `learned of the ground only after the appointment`)

GIVEN `days since notice of the rejection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court challenge is in time` IF
    `days since notice of the rejection` AT MOST 30

§§ `20, 59 -- immunity`

-- s 20: "An arbitrator shall not be liable for (a) negligence in respect of anything done or omitted to be done in the capacity of the
-- arbitrator; or (b) any mistake of law, fact or procedure made in the course of arbitral proceedings or in the making of an arbitral
-- award." Nothing more: s 20 names negligence and mistakes and is silent on dishonesty. That s 20 therefore does not protect
-- deliberate dishonesty is an INFERENCE from its silence.
-- s 59(1): the appointing authority, or an institution or person asked to appoint, "shall not be liable for anything done or omitted
-- in the discharge or purported discharge of that function unless the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith"; (2) not
-- liable "by reason only of having appointed or nominated the arbitrator" for what the arbitrator does.
DECLARE `Claim against an arbitrator` IS ONE OF
    `negligence in conducting the arbitration`
    `a mistake of law in the award`
    `a mistake of fact in the award`
    `a mistake of procedure`
    `deliberate dishonesty`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Claim against an arbitrator`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20 protects the arbitrator` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `deliberate dishonesty` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `shown to be in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claim is only for appointing the arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointing institution is protected` IF
    `the claim is only for appointing the arbitrator` OR (NOT `shown to be in bad faith`)

§§ `21 -- pleas on jurisdiction`

-- s 21(4): "A plea that the arbitral tribunal does not have jurisdiction must be raised not later than the submission of the statement
-- of defence." (5) a party is not precluded "by the fact that the party has appointed, or participated in the appointment of, an
-- arbitrator". (7) despite delay "the arbitral tribunal may admit the plea if it considers the delay to be justified".
-- (9) after a ruling, any party "may, within 30 days after having received notice of that ruling, apply to the Court".
GIVEN `raised by the statement of defence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the tribunal finds the delay justified` IS A BOOLEAN, `the party appointed an arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the jurisdiction plea may be heard` IF
    `raised by the statement of defence` OR `the tribunal finds the delay justified`

GIVEN `days since notice of the ruling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court application on jurisdiction is in time` IF
    `days since notice of the ruling` AT MOST 30

§§ `38, 39 -- reasons and costs`

-- s 38(2): "The award must state the reasons upon which it is based, unless the parties have agreed that no grounds are to be stated or
-- the award is an award on agreed terms under section 37."
-- s 39(2): a provision that a party "must in any event pay their ... own costs of the reference or award ... is void"; (3) except where
-- it "is part of an agreement to submit to arbitration a dispute which has arisen before the making of such agreement".
-- (4) if the award is silent on costs, a party may "within 14 days of the delivery of the award or any further time that the arbitral
-- tribunal may allow" apply for a costs order.
GIVEN `parties agreed no reasons` IS A BOOLEAN, `an award on agreed terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the award must state reasons` IF
    (NOT `parties agreed no reasons`) AND (NOT `an award on agreed terms`)

GIVEN `the dispute had arisen before the agreement was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a pay-your-own-costs clause is void` IF
    NOT `the dispute had arisen before the agreement was made`

GIVEN `days since delivery of the award` IS A NUMBER, `further time allowed by the tribunal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the costs application is in time` IF
    `days since delivery of the award` AT MOST 14 PLUS `further time allowed by the tribunal`

§§ `43 -- correction, interpretation and additional award`

-- s 43(1): "within 30 days of the receipt of the award, unless another period of time has been agreed upon by the parties", a party may
-- (a) request correction of "any error in computation, any clerical or typographical error"; (b) request an interpretation "if the
-- request is also agreed to by the other parties". (4) an additional award for omitted claims, within 30 days of receipt.
DECLARE `Request to the tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `correct a computation or clerical error`
    `interpret a point in the award`
    `make an additional award on an omitted claim`
    `reconsider the merits`

GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request to the tribunal`, `days since receipt of the award` IS A NUMBER, `the other parties agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request may be made under section 43` IF
        `days since receipt of the award` AT MOST 30
    AND CONSIDER `the request`
        WHEN `correct a computation or clerical error` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `make an additional award on an omitted claim` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `interpret a point in the award` THEN `the other parties agree`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `47, 48 -- setting aside`

-- s 47: the Court "does not have jurisdiction to confirm, vary, set aside or remit an award ... except where so provided in this Act".
-- s 48(1)(a): the applicant "proves" (i) incapacity; (ii) agreement not valid; (iii) no proper notice or "otherwise unable to present
-- the party's case"; (iv) award beyond the submission (only the severable excess may be set aside); (v) composition or procedure not
-- as agreed; (vi) "induced or affected by fraud or corruption"; (vii) breach of natural justice by which rights "have been
-- prejudiced". (b) the Court "finds" (i) not arbitrable; (ii) "contrary to public policy".
-- Error of law or fact is not on the list; the route for a question of law is s 49.
DECLARE `Complaint about the award` IS ONE OF
    `a party lacked capacity`
    `the agreement is invalid`
    `no proper notice of the arbitration`
    `the award goes beyond the submission`
    `the tribunal was not constituted as agreed`
    `the award was induced by fraud`
    `a prejudicial breach of natural justice`
    `the dispute is not arbitrable`
    `the award is contrary to public policy`
    `the tribunal got the law wrong`
    `the tribunal got the facts wrong`

GIVEN `the complaint` IS A `Complaint about the award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complaint is a ground for setting aside` IF
    CONSIDER `the complaint`
    WHEN `the tribunal got the law wrong` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the tribunal got the facts wrong` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the complaint` IS A `Complaint about the award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may raise it of its own finding` IF
    CONSIDER `the complaint`
    WHEN `the dispute is not arbitrable` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the award is contrary to public policy` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 48(2): an application "may not be made after the expiry of 3 months from the date on which the party making the application had
-- received the award, or if a request has been made under section 43, from the date on which that request had been disposed of".
-- Months are counted here as a month number (year x 12 + month) and a day of the month; that the period ends on the same day of the
-- month three months later is an INFERENCE (the Act does not say how a month is reckoned here), and month-end cases are not modelled.
GIVEN `start month` IS A NUMBER, `start day` IS A NUMBER, `filing month` IS A NUMBER, `filing day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filed within 3 months` IF
        `filing month` LESS THAN `start month` PLUS 3
    OR  (`filing month` EQUALS `start month` PLUS 3 AND `filing day` AT MOST `start day`)

GIVEN `received month` IS A NUMBER, `received day` IS A NUMBER, `a section 43 request was made` IS A BOOLEAN, `disposed month` IS A NUMBER, `disposed day` IS A NUMBER, `filing month` IS A NUMBER, `filing day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the setting-aside application is in time` IF
    IF `a section 43 request was made`
    THEN `filed within 3 months` `disposed month` `disposed day` `filing month` `filing day`
    ELSE `filed within 3 months` `received month` `received day` `filing month` `filing day`

§§ `49, 50 -- appeal on a question of law`

-- s 49(1): a party may appeal "on a question of law arising out of an award". (2) the parties may exclude this, and "an agreement to
-- dispense with reasons for the arbitral tribunal's award is to be treated as an agreement to exclude the jurisdiction of the Court".
-- (3) only "(a) with the agreement of all the other parties ... or (b) with the permission of the Court". (5) permission "only if"
-- (a) the determination "will substantially affect the rights" of a party; (b) the tribunal "was asked to determine" it; (c) on the
-- findings of fact the decision is "(i) obviously wrong; or (ii) ... of general public importance and ... at least open to serious
-- doubt"; and (d) "it is just and proper in all the circumstances for the Court to determine the question".
-- s 50(2): not until the appellant has exhausted "(a) any available arbitral process of appeal or review; and (b) any available
-- recourse under section 43". (3) "within 28 days of the date of the award or, if there has been any arbitral process of appeal or
-- review, of the date when the applicant or appellant was notified of the result".
-- (7) security for costs is not to be ordered "by reason only" that the appellant is resident or incorporated outside Singapore.
DECLARE `Permission facts` HAS
    `substantially affects the rights of a party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tribunal was asked to determine it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the decision is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of general public importance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least open to serious doubt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `just and proper for the Court to decide` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Permission facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may give permission to appeal` IF
        `the facts`'s `substantially affects the rights of a party`
    AND `the facts`'s `the tribunal was asked to determine it`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the decision is obviously wrong`
         OR  (`the facts`'s `of general public importance` AND `the facts`'s `at least open to serious doubt`))
    AND `the facts`'s `just and proper for the Court to decide`

GIVEN `the parties excluded appeals` IS A BOOLEAN, `the parties dispensed with reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal route is excluded` IF
    `the parties excluded appeals` OR `the parties dispensed with reasons`

GIVEN `days since the start date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filed within 28 days` IF
    `days since the start date` AT MOST 28

GIVEN `excluded` IS A BOOLEAN, `all other parties agree` IS A BOOLEAN, `permission given` IS A BOOLEAN, `arbitral review and section 43 exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the award or the review result` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal on a question of law may be brought` IF
        (NOT `excluded`)
    AND (`all other parties agree` OR `permission given`)
    AND `arbitral review and section 43 exhausted`
    AND `filed within 28 days` `days since the award or the review result`

GIVEN `foreign residence or incorporation is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `security for costs may be ordered on that basis` IF
    NOT `foreign residence or incorporation is the only reason`
